message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Outcome Gates Are Direction Filters"
abstract: >-
  Under mechanically defined edit semantics the space of proposals is finite, so what a
  result-based outcome gate can and cannot see can be counted rather than sampled. Over four
  constructed corpora and four edit semantics, a gate that reads only the outcome admits exactly
  those proposals whose two directions agree, and cannot distinguish a correct edit from a lucky
  one. A closed-form argument and the enumeration agree cell by cell; that agreement is a
  self-consistency check, not an independent validation.
type: preprint
